{100}{}{Ismarc}
{1000}{}{What?
---
Yeah, what do you want?}
{1001}{}{Thanks. What can I do for ya?}
{1002}{}{Oh, great. You don't know how gratified that makes me. Go away.}
{1003}{}{What?!? I don't have time for this.}
{1004}{}{[MANUAL: add NPC dialogue for diagram node 'UpReact']}
{1005}{}{[MANUAL: add NPC dialogue for diagram node 'Ismarc10']}
{1006}{}{Yeah, I sing at the Hub sometimes, and I've visited the Brotherhood of Steel and Adytum
with the caravans. Why do you ask?}
{1007}{}{Hey, thanks. It's hard being a starving artist. You got anything you need to know, you
just ask.
---
I appreciate the thought and all, but you're strapped worse than I am.}
{1008}{}{Ah, I picked it up here and there. Learned a little from an old singer at the Hub, and
got some music from the scavs in Adytum, in the Boneyard. You know. Just takes some
practice.}
{1009}{}{[MANUAL: add NPC dialogue for diagram node 'Ismarc09']}
{1010}{}{The Hub? Oh, it's just a short distance down south of Junktown. What else?}
{1011}{}{The Brotherhood is a couple days west and a little bit north of here. Don't go there,
though. They won't let you in unless you're with a caravan. You need anything else?}
{1012}{}{Hmm. Head southwest of the Hub. Adytum is part of the Boneyard. It's a small,
semi-industrial town. I didn't like it much there. What else do you want?}
{1013}{}{[AUTO-GENERATED SKELETON: replace this entry with the NPC's initial greeting and
conditions.]}
